From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:11:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let Cartouche sign the built-in SideStore in

Cartouche never shows SideStore, so its onboarding's Sign In is out of
the player's reach. A new action, Sign In to Cartouche, runs the same
sign-in without any screen: Cartouche asks for the Apple ID, its
password and the verification code itself, and runs the action in
LiveProcess, as it runs Refresh All Apps; Shortcuts does not list it.

The two processes share SideStore's keychain, and talk through three of
its items: the credentials Cartouche leaves, which the action reads once
and deletes, the verification code request the action leaves when Apple
asks for one, and Cartouche's answer. What SideStore's screens would ask
is decided as the onboarding would have it: the free team, no
certificate revoked, Cartouche not re-signed. An error SideStore would
offer to retry or skip ends the sign-in with that error, and so does an
account Apple asks to repair or an outdated anisette server, for
Cartouche to show.

